WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.210
In 1973 and 1974, the price
of oil roughly quadrupled.

2
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:09.680
Then many rich countries
saw something strange.

3
00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:12.450
Inflation rose. And at the same time,

4
00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:14.370
unemployment rose too.

5
00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:19.050
Normally, when spending booms,
prices climb and jobs grow.

6
00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:23.030
When spending slumps,
prices fall and jobs go.

7
00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:26.560
So how can prices and
unemployment rise together?

8
00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:30.880
In this mission, you'll find where
aggregate demand meets aggregate supply,

9
00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:32.750
and what moves that point.

10
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:36.320
Then you'll hit an economy
with shocks in two graph labs,

11
00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:38.200
and predict what happens to prices,

12
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.040
output and jobs.

13
00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:43.500
Your mission: find out why
prices and unemployment can

14
00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.010
rise at the same time.
